# Project Core

## Spec-Driven Development

- Read `spec/` before implementing. Do not guess requirements.
- If no feature spec exists, create one in `spec/features/` and get user approval first.
- Update specs when requirements change, then update code.

## Version Pins

- Follow `docs/project-versions.md` for all toolchain and dependency versions.
- Do not upgrade major versions without explicit user approval.

## Scope Discipline

- Make the smallest change that solves the request.
- Do not scaffold or build the app unless the user explicitly asks.
- Do not add dependencies without justification.

## Security

- No hardcoded secrets, credentials, or API keys.
- No `eval`, unsafe deserialization, or auth bypasses.
- Validate all user input at API boundaries.

## Structure

- Backend code → `backend/` (when created)
- Frontend code → `frontend/` (when created)
- Specs → `spec/`, docs → `docs/`
